     "page": 1,
     "text": "Morgan-Wong Medical Group\nRe: Carrie Gregory (DOB 03/30/1966)\n\nDr. Michelle Franklin, MD\nGastroenterology\nMorgan-Wong Medical Group\n\nJanuary 17, 2025\n\nThis letter is in response to a recent request from an insurance company regarding the medical status of Mrs. Carrie Gregory, born March 30, 1966. She presented today for a routine flu shot. Her blood pressure at the time of visit was 128/82 mmHg, and her weight was 155 pounds.\n\nMrs. Gregory has a documented history of non-alcoholic fatty liver disease (NAFLD) with liver fibrosis currently at stage F3. She has been under our care since her diagnosis in April 2011. We have been closely monitoring her condition, and it remains controlled. There have been no recent changes in her medication regimen related to her NAFLD. \n\nShe had her last visit on August 15, 2024, when her blood pressure was recorded as 122/79 mmHg, and she weighed 160 pounds. The visit focused on her NAFLD, and her condition remained stable. Her previous visit on March 12, 2024, showed her blood pressure at 122/72 mmHg with a weight of 158 pounds, and she continued to do well.\n\nThe visit on October g, 2023, indicated a blood pressure of 129/71 mmHg, and she weighed 158 pounds. Again, her NAFLD was stable with liver fibrosis at stage F3. On May 6, 2023, her blood pressure was 123/79 mmHg, and her weight was 150 pounds. She presented with stable NAFLD. The 1, 2022, visit recorded her blood pressure as 122/79 mmHg, with a weight of 149 pounds, and her NAFLD remained controlled.\n\nAdditionally, Mrs. Gregory has a history of tobacco use. She was a cigarette smoker, consuming approximately 10 cigarettes per day, starting from October 24, 1989. She stopped smoking on October 19, 2023. She has been honest about her smoking history and cessation.\n\nFamily history is for cardiovascular conditions. Her father had a myocardial infarction (MI) and passed away at the age of 47. Her brother died suddenly from cardiac issues at 52. Her mother also suffered from MI, passing away at 88.\n\nMrs. Gregory has not been documented to have any exercise regimen, and there are no records of alcohol consumption within the past documented visits. \n\nIn summary, Mrs. Gregory's NAFLD with fibrosis stage F3 remains stable and well-controlled. Her cardiovascular risk factors are being managed appropriately. There is no evidence of noncompliance with her treatment plan.\n\nThank you for your attention to these details. Should you require any further information, please do not hesitate to contact us.\n\nSincerely,\n\nDr. Michelle Franklin, MD\nMorgan-Wong Medical Group\n"
    },
    {
     "page": 2,
     "text": "\n[End of Document]\n"
    }
   ],
